**Read:** [Recommendations on the Transport of Dangerous Goods — UN Model Regulations](../sources/Dangerous-Goods-Model-Regulations-UN.lingua#r_608ADXFZHPBDY8MYGJZ9M1BG06), complete relevant classification, package/tank and operation provisions in both volumes; [Transporte rodoviário de produtos perigosos — ANTT](../sources/Transporte-de-Produtos-Perigosos-ANTT.lingua#r_1WNZJ2G2BMBH2YQZ78N09GV8S1), the full applicable consolidated Brazilian regulation and instructions; [Graduate Logistics Systems — MIT ESD.260J](../sources/Graduate-Logistics-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_4NMCCS7JPNK6CD9V9Z4XTQPKR8), the complete transportation/network analysis; [Methanol Safe Handling Manual — Methanol Institute](../sources/Methanol-Safe-Handling-Manual.lingua#r_01VD6M07PMPE9J0W00Z9KD5WC0), the entire transport and storage chapter.

Compare two feasible routes for the same specified chemical and user. Include compatible vehicle/equipment, shipment size, loading/unloading, route access, schedule uncertainty, intermediate handling, acceptance delay and return/residual management. A lower tonne-distance cost can require a different terminal, receiving tank or inventory policy.

Read the complete applicable transport framework and then the exact material-specific entries and provisions. For Brazil use the actual ANTT consolidated text and instructions with their effective dates; distinguish these from the UN model. Determine which party prepares, checks or retains each required piece of information using the actual source, rather than inferring obligations from a diagram.

Calculate one source-to-user service comparison with all quantities and dates declared. Include regular replenishment, a missed delivery window and a changed route. Examine whether the proposed backup uses the same terminal, loading facility or scarce equipment. Study realistic constraints on qualified drivers/operators and receiving hours. The advanced intermodal case extends the model into terminals and marine legs; the generic transport and logistics subjects retain their own full scope beyond this chemical interface.

**Continue:** [Follow a chemical through terminals and intermodal handoffs](Terminals-marine-legs-and-intermodal-packages.lingua#r_2J9HM9CW5PTVNFS003X1KRNT98).

